          <div class="ide">
            <div class="ide-bar">
              <span class="ide-dots"><span class="ide-dot r"></span><span class="ide-dot y"></span><span class="ide-dot g"></span></span>
              <span class="ide-file">ArchitectureTest.java</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="ide-body">classes().that()
  .resideInAPackage(<span class="str">"..domain.."</span>)
  .should().onlyDependOnClassesThat()
  .resideOutsideOfPackage(<span class="str">"..adapters.."</span>)</pre>
          </div>
          <p class="ide-cap"><code>ArchUnit</code>, the original.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="ide-col">
          <span class="lab">JavaScript / TypeScript</span>
          <div class="ide">
            <div class="ide-bar">
              <span class="ide-dots"><span class="ide-dot r"></span><span class="ide-dot y"></span><span class="ide-dot g"></span></span>
              <span class="ide-file">.dependency-cruiser.js</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="ide-body"><span class="key">forbidden</span>: [{
  <span class="key">name</span>: <span class="str">"domain-pure"</span>,
  <span class="key">from</span>: { path: <span class="str">"src/domain"</span> },
  <span class="key">to</span>:   { path: <span class="str">"src/adapters"</span> }
}]</pre>
          </div>
          <p class="ide-cap"><code>dependency-cruiser</code>, or ESLint <code>boundaries</code>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="ide-col">
          <span class="lab">.NET</span>
          <div class="ide">
            <div class="ide-bar">
              <span class="ide-dots"><span class="ide-dot r"></span><span class="ide-dot y"></span><span class="ide-dot g"></span></span>
              <span class="ide-file">ArchitectureTests.cs</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="ide-body">Types.InAssembly(asm)
  .That().ResideInNamespace(<span class="str">"Domain"</span>)
  .ShouldNot()
  .HaveDependencyOn(<span class="str">"Adapters"</span>)</pre>
          </div>
          <p class="ide-cap"><code>NetArchTest</code>, or Roslyn analyzers.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="callout">
        Write the boundary as a rule once, and <strong>CI fails the moment code crosses it</strong>, with no reviewer needed to catch it. The agent reads the failing check and fixes itself, so the structure holds without you policing every diff.
      </div>
